# name: test_merge_main_failure_routes_recovery_to_live_builder
  '''
  MERGE MAIN RECOVERY REQUIRED: prepared-work
  
  The work state machine hit a recoverable worktree merge failure before it could continue.
  
  Execute in order:
  
  telec sessions send builder-session 'The work state machine failed while merging origin/main into your worktree for prepared-work. You did not encounter this directly; the orchestrator is routing the machine-owned failure back to you.
  
  Recover the worktree: preserve accepted origin/main behavior as the leading baseline, reapply this todo'"'"'s prepared intent from implementation-plan and PRD/input on top, resolve the conflicts, run relevant focused tests plus telec code test and telec code lint, commit the resolution, then run `telec todo stamp prepared-work --build-complete` and report completion.
  
  State-machine merge failure:
  conflict details'
  
  Cancel your existing backup heartbeat timer, then start a fresh 300-second one the same way — your runtime's own non-blocking timer mechanism, per the non-blocking Heartbeat policy (never hold a tool call open, never block user input). The timer is a bare, fire-once delay that re-engages your judgment — never a condition test, never a tighter interval.
  When the builder reports idle after re-stamping, call telec todo work prepared-work.
  '''
# ---
# name: test_prepared_entry_advances_to_build_started_without_removed_phase_commands
  'BUILD_START_DISPATCH: prepared-work'
